studying AI and not using AI. Perhaps as somebody who studies skills and performance and offloading, I'm sort of just not willing to offload at this point. That might change, I might just be, you know. Resisting the inevitable. Right, exactly, exactly. So we'll see. But I don't want to come across as just sort of anti any kind of new technology because I think there are absolutely benefits that come with it. What are you working on now? What are the big questions that you're trying to answer? So one of the questions that I'm working on with colleagues from computer science and medicine and robotics is looking at AI skill development, particularly in radiology and surgical robotics, skilled maintenance in those areas. So do we see skill decay?

